{"sections":[],"topicSections":[{"title":"The bundle","anchor":"The-bundle","identifiers":["doc:\/\/GnustoSpellcasting\/documentation\/GnustoSpellcasting\/Spellcasting","doc:\/\/GnustoSpellcasting\/documentation\/GnustoSpellcasting\/Spellcasting\/init(memorySlots:maxMana:)","doc:\/\/GnustoSpellcasting\/documentation\/GnustoSpellcasting\/Spellcasting\/memorySlots","doc:\/\/GnustoSpellcasting\/documentation\/GnustoSpellcasting\/Spellcasting\/maxMana"]},{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/GnustoSpellcasting\/documentation\/GnustoSpellcasting\/Spellcasting\/spell(_:cost:effect:)"],"anchor":"Registering-a-spell","title":"Registering a spell"},{"anchor":"The-four-paradigms","title":"The four paradigms","identifiers":["doc:\/\/GnustoSpellcasting\/documentation\/GnustoSpellcasting\/SpellCost","doc:\/\/GnustoSpellcasting\/documentation\/GnustoSpellcasting\/SpellCost\/cantrip","doc:\/\/GnustoSpellcasting\/documentation\/GnustoSpellcasting\/SpellCost\/prepared(book:learnVia:)","doc:\/\/GnustoSpellcasting\/documentation\/GnustoSpellcasting\/SpellCost\/energy(_:)","doc:\/\/GnustoSpellcasting\/documentation\/GnustoSpellcasting\/SpellCost\/scroll(_:)"]},{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/GnustoSpellcasting\/documentation\/GnustoSpellcasting\/Spellcasting\/verbs","doc:\/\/GnustoSpellcasting\/documentation\/GnustoSpellcasting\/Spellcasting\/actions","doc:\/\/GnustoSpellcasting\/documentation\/GnustoSpellcasting\/Spellcasting\/noiseWords"],"anchor":"What-the-bundle-contributes-to-the-host","title":"What the bundle contributes to the host"},{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/GnustoSpellcasting\/documentation\/GnustoSpellcasting\/Gnusto"],"generated":true,"anchor":"Extended-Modules","title":"Extended Modules"}],"abstract":[{"text":"Four ways a spell becomes available, over one way of writing what it does.","type":"text"}],"metadata":{"title":"GnustoSpellcasting","externalID":"GnustoSpellcasting","roleHeading":"Framework","role":"collection","symbolKind":"module","modules":[{"name":"GnustoSpellcasting"}]},"kind":"symbol","schemaVersion":{"major":0,"patch":0,"minor":3},"primaryContentSections":[{"content":[{"type":"heading","text":"Overview","level":2,"anchor":"Overview"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Magic systems differ in their bookkeeping, not in their effects. An at-will"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"cantrip, a spell memorized from a book and spent in the speaking, a bolt paid"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"for out of an energy pool, and a scroll good for one reading all do the same"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"sort of thing to the world; what separates them is when the game says no. This"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"library keeps the two apart. A spell’s effect is an ordinary rule body, written"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"exactly as any other rule body is, and a ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/GnustoSpellcasting\/documentation\/GnustoSpellcasting\/SpellCost","type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":" sits beside it deciding"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"availability and price."}]},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A spell’s identity is its own intent, declared with "},{"code":"#verb","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" like any custom"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"verb, so "},{"code":"glow","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"cast glow"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"code":"read passwall","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" are parser rows and a spell can"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"carry as many phrasings as its author wants. "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/GnustoSpellcasting\/documentation\/GnustoSpellcasting\/Spellcasting\/spell(_:cost:effect:)"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"returns the actions that intent needs — the cast handler, plus the memorize"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"handler when the cost is ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/GnustoSpellcasting\/documentation\/GnustoSpellcasting\/SpellCost\/prepared(book:learnVia:)","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":" — and the game"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"splices them into its "},{"code":"actions","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" block.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"It is a "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"GameContent"},{"text":" bundle rather than a ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"GamePlugin"},{"type":"text","text":", because it has state to"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"save. The finite spell memory and the energy pool are "},{"code":"@Global","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"s it owns, so","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"both travel in a save and come back correctly under UNDO; the defaults are 3","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"slots and 12 mana. Everything else is the host’s: the spellbook, the scroll, the","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"targets, and every word of prose an effect prints. The bundle contributes two","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"verbs of its own — "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"rest"},{"type":"text","text":" (or "},{"code":"meditate","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"), which refills the pool, and ","type":"text"},{"code":"spells","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"(or ","type":"text"},{"code":"magic","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"), which reports what is held in mind and how much energy is left —","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"and adds ","type":"text"},{"code":"spell","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" to the parser’s noise words, so ","type":"text"},{"code":"cast the glow spell","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" reaches","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"glow","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":".","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Casting runs gate, effect, pay. Availability is checked first; the effect runs"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"second and may refuse on its own account with "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"require"},{"type":"text","text":" or "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"reply"},{"type":"text","text":"; only an"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"effect that finished pays. So a firebolt aimed at nothing costs no energy, and a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"scroll read at the wrong wall survives."}]},{"type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Wiring it in","anchor":"Wiring-it-in"},{"code":["import Gnusto","import GnustoSpellcasting","","extension Intent {","    #verb(\"glow\", [\"glow\"], [\"cast\", \"glow\"])","    #verb(","        \"firebolt\", [\"firebolt\"], [\"cast\", \"firebolt\"],","        [\"firebolt\", .directObject], [\"cast\", \"firebolt\", \"at\", .directObject])","}","","struct Tower: Game {","    let magic = Spellcasting(memorySlots: 3, maxMana: 12)","","    var content: GameContents { magic }","    var verbs: [SyntaxRule] { [.glow, .firebolt] }","","    var actions: [IntentAction] {","        magic.spell(.glow, cost: .cantrip) {","            say(\"Pale light seeps from your fingers.\")","        }","        magic.spell(.firebolt, cost: .energy(4)) {","            guard let target = command.directObject else {","                try reply(\"Cast firebolt at what?\")","            }","            target.vanish()","            say(\"Fire leaps from your hand and bursts against \\(target.definiteName).\")","        }","    }","}"],"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/GnustoSpellcasting\/documentation\/GnustoSpellcasting\/SpellCost\/prepared(book:learnVia:)","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" spell carries its own memorize intent,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"so the one "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"spell(_:cost:effect:)"},{"type":"text","text":" call registers both halves:"}]},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["magic.spell(.unbar, cost: .prepared(book: spellbook, learnVia: .learnUnbar)) {","    try require(!wardedDoor.isOpen, else: \"The door already stands open.\")","    wardedDoor.isOpen = true","    say(\"The warding-marks gutter and die, and the door drifts open.\")","}"]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Pass "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"book: nil"},{"type":"text","text":" and the spell can be memorized anywhere; pass an item and it"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"has to be in hand.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"heading","level":2,"text":"The worked example","anchor":"The-worked-example"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Sources\/Gramarye\/"},{"type":"text","text":" is a small original game built to test the claim in the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"first sentence of this page. It runs one spell per paradigm and chains them so"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":"each opens exactly one obstacle: the cantrip finds the scroll, the memorized"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":"spell opens the warded door, the energy spell destroys the golem, the scroll"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"passes the wall. Remove any one of the four and the amulet is unreachable, which","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"is a stronger demonstration than four spells that happen to work. Its design","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"document is ","type":"text"},{"code":"docs\/games\/gramarye.md","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":".","type":"text"}]}],"kind":"content"}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[[]]},"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/gnusto